yaml/key-value-pair
description: A key and a value separated by a colon; node properties may precede the value
- >
  A key and a value separated by a colon and a space. Leaving the value empty means null - the
  bare key IS the null. Between the colon and the value a pair may carry the node's
  PROPERTIES - an **anchor** and/or a **tag**:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  age: 42
  boss: &chief
    name: Rex
  count: !!int '42'
- >
  The key, the anchor, and the tag have subchapters below; the value can be ANY YAML value -
  the grammar recurses here:
- *: 00-yaml_key
- *: 01-yaml_anchor
- *: 02-yaml_tag
- *..:..:..
